<!--
  Athex Oasis Ids relaxed channel, version 5.2 (ATHEX OASIS IDS Market Data Feed Specification
  5.2, Table 3-4 and chapter 5). The channel carries what is not produced directly by the Oasis
  matching engine, dispatched by the same Message Category of the same Ids header the real time
  channel uses, which Ids.Header.Tcp.Source.xml declares.

  Two of the four categories Table 3-4 lists are transcribed, because they are the two the
  document gives a format for:

  - U, the Apa Post Trade Message of Table 5-1, and V, the Apa Pre-trade Message of Table 5-2,
    both 699 characters, both for the Mifid II Apa transparency service.
  - W, a Closing/Fixing Price Message, has no format anywhere in the document. Its section 5.1
    heading and its Table 5-1 caption are both the Word error "Error! Bookmark not defined.",
    and the section that should hold it carries the field characteristics of U and V instead.
  - T, an OTC Message, is listed in Table 3-4 and nowhere else. No field table, no section.

  Neither W nor T is authored: the document states no layout for either, and inventing one would
  dissect bytes it never described. Both are open questions for the publisher.

  The Req column marks a field required or conditionally required. A conditionally required field
  still occupies its full width - section 5.1 states null as n spaces for an alphanumeric field
  and n zeroes for a numeric one - so nothing here is optional on the wire, which is what makes
  both messages a fixed 699 characters.

  A {DECIMAL-n/m} writes its own decimal point and omits the fraction entirely when there is
  none, so these fields state their own places rather than implying a fixed scale.

  Three fields carry a documented value list that is deliberately not authored as a value set,
  because the codes are narrower than the field and no enum on it could ever match:

  - Underlying index name is twenty five characters holding either a four character index code
    from the section 5.1 {INDEX} list or free text.
  - Term of the underlying index is seven characters, three of term and four of unit.
  - OTC Post-trade indicator is a four character bitmap of thirteen flags, which combine.

  Each states its codes in its own description instead.
-->

